{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 ReaPackLab\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 ReaPackLab is a fork of ReaPack designed for managed REAPER environments.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 This package currently provides a macOS Apple Silicon binary. It is a development-era build of the centrally managed edition, not the separate stateless ReaPackLabSetup bootstrap extension. Use in a clean test REAPER installation before classroom deployment.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Based on ReaPack by Christian Fillion (LGPL-3.0-or-later).\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 ReaPackLab\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b ReaPackLab} is the release repository for the REAPER extension in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/rockumk"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
ReaLab
}}}
 project. It is based on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://reapack.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
ReaPack
}}}
, the package manager created by Christian Fillion.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The published v0.14.0 binary is a development-era {\b centrally managed} ReaPackLab build, with hosted configuration and Teacher Mode. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/rockumk/ReaPackLabDev"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
ReaPackLabDev
}}}
 is its source and development repository. The planned permanently restricted, single-repository bootstrap variant is a separate project, {\b ReaPackLabSetup}, and is not included here.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li720 \fi0 {\b Initial release:} {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/rockumk/ReaPackLab/releases/tag/v0.14.0"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
v0.14.0
}}}
 provides a macOS Apple Silicon ({\f1 darwin-arm64}) binary. It should be tested in an isolated REAPER installation before wider deployment; other platforms are not yet listed.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Repository\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 This repository follows the standard {\f1 reapack-index} layout:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 ReaPackLab/\line
\u9500 ?\u9472 ?\u9472 ? index.xml             # Generated ReaPack index\line
\u9500 ?\u9472 ?\u9472 ? Extensions/           # Extension package metadata (.ext)\line
\u9500 ?\u9472 ?\u9472 ? README.md             # Repository description\line
\u9492 ?\u9472 ?\u9472 ? .github/workflows/    # Index checks and generation\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Repository index URL:}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rockumk/ReaPackLab/master/index.xml\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The index is generated automatically by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/cfillion/reapack-index"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
reapack-index
}}}
 after package metadata is added. Do not edit generated package entries in {\f1 index.xml} by hand. Currently, the index has a macOS Apple Silicon package for v0.14.0.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Extension packaging\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Native REAPER extensions are described by a metadata file such as {\f1 Extensions/ReaPackLab.ext}. The {\f1 @provides} entries tell ReaPack which binary to download for each operating system and architecture. Their target filenames are installed into REAPER's {\f1 UserPlugins} directory.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 See {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "Extensions/README.md"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
Extensions/README.md
}}}
 for the release metadata template and conventions based on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/ReaTeam/Extensions"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
ReaTeam/Extensions
}}}
, including {\f1 darwin-arm64}, {\f1 darwin64}, {\f1 win64}, and {\f1 linux64}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A package version must never be published before all URLs in its active {\f1 @provides} entries point to verified release assets. GitHub Actions build artifacts are not the same as stable release assets.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Relationship to ReaPackLabDev\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 | Project | Role | | --- | --- | | {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/rockumk/ReaPackLab"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
ReaPackLab
}}}
 | Release repository for the managed extension | | {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/rockumk/ReaPackLabDev"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
ReaPackLabDev
}}}
 | Source and development of the managed extension | | ReaLab | Umbrella name for the broader software project |\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The two extension variants should be tested in separate REAPER resource directories to avoid competing over package files.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 License and acknowledgments\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 ReaPackLab is derived from ReaPack by Christian Fillion. ReaPack is licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 3 or later. Derived source and binaries must retain the applicable license and attribution notices. Packaging tools and repository-format documentation are provided by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/cfillion/reapack-index"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
ReaPack
}}}
 ecosystem.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 ReaPackLab is an independent project and is not affiliated with Cockos, Inc.\par}
}
